2025-08-31 17:48:33,950 - INFO - Function Requirement: Function Name: validate_us_phone_number  
Description: Validates whether a given string is a valid US phone number. Supports formats such as  
  - (555) 123-4567  
  - 555-123-4567  
  - 1234567890  
Parameters:  
  - number (string): The phone number to validate.  
Returns:  
  - boolean: true if the number is a valid US phone number, false otherwise.  
Example Implementation (JavaScript):  
```javascript
function validate_us_phone_number(number) {
  // US phone number regex:
  // Optional parentheses around area code, optional separators (space or hyphen)
  const regex = /^\(?\d{3}\)?[- ]?\d{3}[- ]?\d{4}$/;
  return regex.test(number);
}

// Example validations:
console.log(validate_us_phone_number("(555) 123-4567")); // true
console.log(validate_us_phone_number("555-123-4567"));   // true
console.log(validate_us_phone_number("1234567890"));     // true
console.log(validate_us_phone_number("555123456"));      // false
```
