2025-09-01 23:03:37,307 - INFO - Function Requirement: Function Name: advanced_matrix_ops  
Description: Uses the existing `matrix_operations` function to perform matrix multiplication (when requested), computes eigenvalues of the resulting matrix (or of an input matrix), and caches any intermediate or final results in a global `computation_cache` object to avoid redundant computation.  
Parameters:  
- a: two-dimensional array of numbers  
  • The first input matrix.  
- b (optional): two-dimensional array of numbers  
  • The second input matrix to multiply with `a`. Required only if multiplication is requested.  
- compute_product: boolean  
  • If true, multiply `a` by `b` using `matrix_operations`.  
- compute_eigenvalues: boolean  
  • If true, compute the eigenvalues of the matrix (either the product `a × b` if `compute_product` is true, or of `a` otherwise).  
- cache: object  
  • A reference to the `computation_cache` variable where results will be stored and looked up.  
Return:  
An object containing any of the following, depending on which flags were set:  
- product: the matrix product of `a` and `b`  
- eigenvalues: an array of eigenvalues  
- from_cache: boolean indicating whether the eigenvalues or product were retrieved from cache  

Example Usage:  
```javascript
// Assume computation_cache is a global object already defined in the session:
let computation_cache = {};

// Call advanced_matrix_ops to multiply matrices and get eigenvalues:
const result = advanced_matrix_ops({
  a: [[1,2],[3,4]],
  b: [[5,6],[7,8]],
  compute_product: true,
  compute_eigenvalues: true,
  cache: computation_cache
});

// Possible result:
// {
//   product: [[19,22],[43,50]],
//   eigenvalues: [69.2965, -0.2965],
//   from_cache: false
// }
```
